The resources/instances.json file was generated by the gce_instance_gen tool
located at https://github.com/google-octo/gcp_instance_gen/tree/main

All recommendations and pricing utilize the bundled `resources/instances.json`
catalog reflecting `us-central1` list pricing.

## Example Use Cases & Questions

Users can leverage the `gce-instance-selector` skill by asking questions about
hardware sizing, price-performance tradeoffs, storage limits, and regional
costs:

-   **Storage:**

    -   *"Tell me which instance type in gcp delivers the best price per
        hyperdisk balanced to deliver at least 100GB/s."*
    -   *"Tell me which instance type in gcp delivers the best price per network
        egress bandwidth. The instance should support at least 32Gbps"*
    -   *"Which machine types in gcp support 100,000+ IOPS on Hyperdisk Extreme,
        and what is their estimated monthly cost?"*
    -   *"Which storage type delivers the highest IOPs for a c3-standard-88 in
        gcp ?"*

-   **Compute Sizing & Architecture:**

    -   *"Find the cheapest ARM-based instance in gcp with at least 32 vCPUs and
        128 GiB of RAM."*
    -   *"Recommend x86 machine types in gcp with 16 vCPUs and 64 GiB RAM,
        ranked from newest generation to oldest."*

-   **Pricing Models & Regional Comparisons:**

    -   *"Compare Spot, On-Demand, and 1-year CUD pricing for c3-standard-8 in
        gcp."*

-   **Networking & Accelerators:**

    -   *"Which instance shapes support at least 100 Gbps egress bandwidth in
        gcp ?"*
    -   *"Show me GPU-accelerated instances in gcp with local NVMe SSD scratch
        disks."*
    -   *"Show me the networking egress bandwidth of all TPU-accelerated
        instances in gcp."*

All data is generated on a best effort basis. Please refer to the pricing
api and public GCP webpages for official information.

Please contact hildebrand@google.com for access, feature requests, etc.
